					"diagramNodeId": "efcce7e5-1cc9-44ef-9f3e-0267f3d8e61c",
					"simStepLabel": "File Filtering Flow: Walker Skips or Yields Entry",
					"simStepDescription": "Based on the final decision, the walker either skips the current file/directory or yields it as a result to be searched.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/ignore/src/walk.rs",
						"startLine": "1130",
						"endLine": "1139",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"Walk::next",
							"self.skip_entry",
							"should_skip_entry"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"MatchResult\": \"Ignore(Hidden)\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"action\": \"skip_entry\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "94371253-20a9-4bdd-804c-a3defb50205c",
					"diagramNodeId": "c5edbe5d-c942-47d6-b464-8d24d32bd4b9",
					"simStepLabel": "Binary Detection Flow: Configure Searcher",
					"simStepDescription": "For files that are not filtered out, a search worker is configured. By default (`-uuu` or `--binary` not specified), it uses implicit binary detection, which is configured to stop searching a file if a `NUL` (\\x00) byte is found.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/search.rs",
						"startLine": "138",
						"endLine": "146",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"binary_detection_implicit",
							"self.config.binary_implicit",
							"grep::searcher::BinaryDetection"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"args\": {\"binary\": \"Auto\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"config\": {\"binary_implicit\": \"Quit(0)\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "5f11c073-1322-447e-b02e-c1a2af1486b2",
					"diagramNodeId": "149dcef9-f96c-43f7-929c-23413d0e8a91",
					"simStepLabel": "Binary Detection Flow: Prepare Line Buffer",
					"simStepDescription": "The `BinaryDetection` configuration is passed to the `Searcher`, which in turn configures the `LineBuffer` that will read the file's contents.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/searcher/src/searcher/mod.rs",
						"startLine": "506",
						"endLine": "514",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"SearcherBuilder::binary_detection",
							"self.config.binary"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"config\": {\"binary_implicit\": \"Quit(0)\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"config\": {\"binary_implicit\": \"Quit(0)\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "786d36e5-52b9-428a-af4e-0e65cee1bab9",
					"diagramNodeId": "8ece57d2-6f37-42c4-aba9-0db00edd4778",
					"simStepLabel": "Binary Detection Flow: Detect NUL Byte",
					"simStepDescription": "As the `LineBufferReader` reads chunks of the file, it scans for the configured binary-detection byte. By default, this is the `NUL` byte (`\\x00`). If this byte is found, the read operation stops.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/searcher/src/line_buffer.rs",
						"startLine": "192",
						"endLine": "200",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"LineBufferBuilder::binary_detection",
							"BinaryDetection",
							"BinaryDetection::Quit"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"file_chunk\": \"some text\\u0000and more\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"binary_detected\": true, \"offset\": 10}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "987d43f3-ac7a-4a1b-aa29-6d888da7cfd7",
					"diagramNodeId": "565af3ba-7954-409d-a197-83965385f34b",
					"simStepLabel": "Binary Detection Flow: Signal Binary File",
					"simStepDescription": "The `LineBufferReader` signals back to the `Searcher` that binary data was detected at a specific byte offset. The `Searcher` then communicates this to the `Sink` (printer).",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/printer/src/standard.rs",
						"startLine": "824",
						"endLine": "824",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"sink.binary_data"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"binary_detected\": true, \"offset\": 10}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"binary_detected\": true, \"offset\": 10}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ed897cb1-4622-4c1d-ab3c-3e88b147fd16",
					"diagramNodeId": "f096b26b-a993-448f-9764-7c56299ae181",
					"simStepLabel": "Binary Detection Flow: Stop Searching and Report",
					"simStepDescription": "The printer's sink receives the `binary_data` signal. It stops further processing of the file and, depending on other flags, may print a message like `Binary file (standard input) matches` if a match was found before the NUL byte.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/printer/src/standard.rs",
						"startLine": "824",
						"endLine": "832",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"sink.binary_data",
							"searcher.binary_detection()",
							"quit_byte()",
							"log::debug!"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"path\": \"/path/to/binary/file\", \"binary_byte_offset\": 10}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"action\": \"stop_processing_file\", \"log_message\": \"ignoring /path/to/binary/file: found binary data at offset 10\"}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- By default, respects rules in <code></li><li>gitignore</code>, <code></li><li>ignore</code>, and <code></li><li>rgignore</code> files to exclude irrelevant files from search results</li><li>- Skips hidden files and directories (those starting with a <code></li><li></code>) by default, focusing the search on source code</li><li>- Automatically skips binary files by detecting NULL bytes to prevent garbled output and improve relevance</li><li>- This behavior is primarily managed by the <code>ignore</code> crate's <code>WalkBuilder</code> and <code>BinaryDetection</code> in <code>grep-searcher</code>, and can be disabled with <code>-u</code> flags</li></ul>",
