		"Manually include or exclude specific files and file types from a search": {
			"name": "Manually include or exclude specific files and file types from a search",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "6dc9840e-c33e-4483-bd88-e650fabd9c51",
					"diagramNodeId": "c0e8b1c4-e191-4211-aad4-6be88b92a072",
					"simStepLabel": "Parse Command-Line Arguments",
					"simStepDescription": "Ripgrep starts by parsing the command-line arguments provided by the user. Flags like `--glob` (`-g`), `--type` (`-t`), `--type-not` (`-T`), and `--type-add` are recognized and their values are collected into a temporary `LowArgs` structure.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/defs.rs",
						"startLine": "2504",
						"endLine": "2572",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"Glob",
							"Flag::update",
							"args.globs"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "rg 'fn' -g '*.rs' -g '!src/main.rs' --type-add 'rust:*.rs' -t rust -T toml",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"globs\": [\n    \"*.rs\",\n    \"!src/main.rs\"\n  ],\n  \"type_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Add\",\n      \"def\": \"rust:*.rs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Select\",\n      \"name\": \"rust\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Negate\",\n      \"name\": \"toml\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "18184e88-837a-4e4d-b824-bc371595d42e",
					"diagramNodeId": "4373def2-f4db-41fc-94b4-238b72df32ce",
					"simStepLabel": "Low-level to High-level Argument Conversion",
					"simStepDescription": "The parsed `LowArgs` structure, containing simple collections of strings and enums, is passed to a constructor to create a `HiArgs` structure. This conversion process builds more complex objects like glob and type matchers.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "111",
						"endLine": "111",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"HiArgs::from_low_args"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"globs\": [\n    \"*.rs\",\n    \"!src/main.rs\"\n  ],\n  \"type_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Add\",\n      \"def\": \"rust:*.rs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Select\",\n      \"name\": \"rust\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Negate\",\n      \"name\": \"toml\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"globs\": [\n    \"*.rs\",\n    \"!src/main.rs\"\n  ],\n  \"type_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Add\",\n      \"def\": \"rust:*.rs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Select\",\n      \"name\": \"rust\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"Negate\",\n      \"name\": \"toml\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ae5710b2-b742-4996-acee-51055fa1bff6",
					"diagramNodeId": "3ffa4ee8-16b5-4a7b-81d6-b67fa0d4902e",
					"simStepLabel": "Build Glob Override Matcher",
					"simStepDescription": "The `globs` function is called to process glob patterns from `-g` and `--iglob`. It uses `ignore::overrides::OverrideBuilder` to construct a high-priority filter. This builder will interpret globs starting with `!` as exclusion patterns.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "1214",
						"endLine": "1225",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"globs",
							"ignore::overrides::OverrideBuilder",
							"low.globs",
							"low.iglobs",
							"builder.add(glob)"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"globs\": [\n    \"*.rs\",\n    \"!src/main.rs\"\n  ],\n  \"iglobs\": [],\n  \"glob_case_insensitive\": false\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"builder\": \"ignore::overrides::OverrideBuilder\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d2788fc8-9f77-477b-b66a-8a3a0256d495",
					"diagramNodeId": "907e6e6c-2343-4711-9a97-43fe6d3a5028",
					"simStepLabel": "Add Raw Globs to Builder",
					"simStepDescription": "Each glob pattern string provided by the user is passed to the `OverrideBuilder`.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/ignore/src/overrides.rs",
						"startLine": "149",
						"endLine": "152",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"OverrideBuilder::add",
							"self.builder.add_line"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "\"!src/main.rs\"",
					"outputDataExample": "\"!src/main.rs\""
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "62db2008-5759-4d9c-b784-cc1af83fc022",
					"diagramNodeId": "8fcf5028-964d-4098-af80-f840077566fd",
					"simStepLabel": "Parse and Process Individual Globs",
					"simStepDescription": "Inside the `ignore` crate, `GitignoreBuilder::add_line` processes each glob string. It applies `.gitignore` semantics, such as prepending `**/` to patterns without a path separator to allow them to match at any directory depth. It then uses `globset::GlobBuilder` to parse the glob into a structured format.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/ignore/src/gitignore.rs",
						"startLine": "449",
						"endLine": "528",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"GitignoreBuilder::add_line",
							"GlobBuilder::new",
							"glob.actual"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "\"!src/main.rs\"",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"glob\": {\n    \"original\": \"!src/main.rs\",\n    \"actual\": \"src/main.rs\",\n    \"is_whitelist\": false\n  }\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "cbc04ec5-7f3b-41ea-aff0-a227894d84d4",
					"diagramNodeId": "e438d533-3d6a-4b67-b71c-401a36231f57",
					"simStepLabel": "Collect Processed Globs",
					"simStepDescription": "The parsed and compiled `globset::Glob` object for each pattern is added to a `GlobSetBuilder`, which prepares to combine them into an efficient, multi-pattern matcher.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/ignore/src/gitignore.rs",
						"startLine": "529",
						"endLine": "529",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"self.builder.add(parsed)"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\n  \"glob\": \"globset::Glob(\\\"src/main.rs\\\")\"\n}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\n  \"glob\": \"globset::Glob(\\\"src/main.rs\\\")\"\n}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "7ad608c3-dcaa-4ea6-9174-e68e0eb9b2cc",
					"diagramNodeId": "213cea68-d7ad-48dd-8dd7-00bca6be9fe0",
					"simStepLabel": "Finalize Override Matcher",
					"simStepDescription": "The `OverrideBuilder`'s `build` method is called. This internally calls `GlobSetBuilder::build`, which compiles all the individual globs into a single, highly optimized `GlobSet` matcher. This final `Override` object is stored in the `HiArgs` struct.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/ignore/src/overrides.rs",
						"startLine": "131",
						"endLine": "133",
						"relevantVariables": [
