		"High-performance parallel searching using multi-threading and memory maps": {
			"name": "High-performance parallel searching using multi-threading and memory maps",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "75c2e235-6f3d-4b06-8b04-2483afc3099e",
					"diagramNodeId": "66293298-c3cb-4599-bcd5-e7953b5d7dd4",
					"simStepLabel": "Argument Parsing and Mmap Mode Configuration",
					"simStepDescription": "The application starts and parses command-line arguments. When the user provides the `--mmap` flag, it updates the `mmap` field in the `LowArgs` struct to `MmapMode::AlwaysTryMmap`, indicating a preference for using memory maps.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/defs.rs",
						"startLine": "4092",
						"endLine": "4099",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"Mmap",
							"Flag",
							"update",
							"args.mmap",
							"MmapMode::AlwaysTryMmap",
							"MmapMode::Never"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"args\": [\"rg\", \"--mmap\", \"-i\", \"error\", \"./logs\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"mmap\": \"AlwaysTryMmap\", \"patterns\": [\"error\"], \"paths\": [\"./logs\"], \"case_mode\": \"Smart\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "45bdcfba-93f7-422b-9d35-09081ebb404e",
					"diagramNodeId": "cb5aebde-56ce-465a-ad14-778478e1d656",
					"simStepLabel": "Low-Level to High-Level Argument Conversion",
					"simStepDescription": "The parsed low-level arguments (`LowArgs`) are passed to a conversion function to create a more structured high-level representation (`HiArgs`) that is easier for the core application logic to use.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "161",
						"endLine": "161",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"HiArgs::from_low"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"mmap\": \"AlwaysTryMmap\", \"patterns\": [\"error\"], \"paths\": [\"./logs\"], \"threads\": 8}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"mmap\": \"AlwaysTryMmap\", \"patterns\": [\"error\"], \"paths\": [\"./logs\"], \"threads\": 8}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "7521380f-7d32-4e5b-9db7-7283fc5a1849",
					"diagramNodeId": "84746b22-cd66-4264-951b-93cbfcfcec4e",
					"simStepLabel": "Mmap Strategy Determination",
					"simStepDescription": "The `HiArgs::from_low` constructor analyzes the `MmapMode`. Since it is `AlwaysTryMmap`, it sets the `mmap_choice` to `grep::searcher::MmapChoice::auto()`. This enables the searcher to attempt using memory maps, but the final decision is still based on heuristics (e.g., file size). If `MmapMode` were `Auto`, it would only use `mmap` if a small number of files were provided directly.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "227",
						"endLine": "250",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"mmap_choice",
							"MmapMode::Auto",
							"MmapMode::AlwaysTryMmap",
							"MmapMode::Never",
							"grep::searcher::MmapChoice::auto()",
							"grep::searcher::MmapChoice::never()"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"low_args\": {\"mmap\": \"AlwaysTryMmap\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"hi_args\": {\"mmap_choice\": \"MmapChoice::auto()\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a84c9cfc-7d69-40a7-b0c4-05cfae4cf433",
					"diagramNodeId": "4f260272-c6cd-467f-b4d4-93c296782e2c",
					"simStepLabel": "Passing High-Level Config to Execution Logic",
					"simStepDescription": "The fully configured `HiArgs` object, now containing the `MmapChoice`, is passed to the main `run` function which orchestrates the search.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/main.rs",
						"startLine": "80",
						"endLine": "80",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"args"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"HiArgs\": {\"mmap_choice\": \"MmapChoice::auto()\", \"threads\": 8}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"HiArgs\": {\"mmap_choice\": \"MmapChoice::auto()\", \"threads\": 8}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f59f7cc3-b38d-40b8-8cbf-5631eae02b01",
					"diagramNodeId": "b89c98dc-23d9-4cce-9be4-536ca9171466",
					"simStepLabel": "Dispatch to Parallel Search",
					"simStepDescription": "The main `run` function checks the number of configured threads. Since it is greater than one, it dispatches the execution to `search_parallel`, the function responsible for multi-threaded searching.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/main.rs",
						"startLine": "86",
						"endLine": "87",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"args.mode()",
							"args.threads()",
							"search_parallel"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"args\": {\"mode\": \"Search\", \"threads\": 8}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"function_call\": \"search_parallel\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "aee911c8-133d-4e18-96f8-c0c17ce79bc5",
					"diagramNodeId": "01d631f3-22b2-488d-98e7-7308d65cc727",
					"simStepLabel": "Invoking Parallel Search",
					"simStepDescription": "The `HiArgs` configuration is passed to the `search_parallel` function to begin the directory traversal and search.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/main.rs",
						"startLine": "87",
						"endLine": "87",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"search_parallel",
							"args"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"HiArgs\": {\"mmap_choice\": \"MmapChoice::auto()\", \"threads\": 8}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"HiArgs\": {\"mmap_choice\": \"MmapChoice::auto()\", \"threads\": 8}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "865bde1f-4ad4-48a7-ac16-5c18982c9b6e",
					"diagramNodeId": "ce78aee4-28b0-48aa-9dcd-cea1499fe055",
					"simStepLabel": "Build Parallel Directory Walker",
					"simStepDescription": "Inside `search_parallel`, a `WalkParallel` instance is created using `args.walk_builder()`. This component, from the `ignore` crate, is responsible for recursively walking the directory tree across multiple threads while respecting ignore files (`.gitignore`, etc.).",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/ignore/src/walk.rs",
						"startLine": "595",
						"endLine": "595",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"WalkBuilder",
							"build_parallel",
							"WalkParallel"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"walk_builder_config\": {\"threads\": 8, \"respect_ignore_files\": true}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"WalkParallel\": {\"status\": \"initialized\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "e4ab2591-123b-4226-9dce-0bf698044e39",
					"diagramNodeId": "22408ca7-b743-48fb-8695-aeff33a3c2e7",
					"simStepLabel": "Distributing File Paths to Worker Threads",
					"simStepDescription": "The `WalkParallel` instance's `run` method is called with a closure. The walker traverses directories and sends `DirEntry` results for each file to a pool of worker threads managed by `crossbeam`.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/main.rs",
						"startLine": "175",
						"endLine": "189",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"build_parallel",
							"run",
							"worker",
							"haystack_builder"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"DirEntry\": {\"path\": \"./logs/app-2023-10-27.log\", \"file_type\": \"file\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"DirEntry\": {\"path\": \"./logs/app-2023-10-27.log\", \"file_type\": \"file\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d2470e87-a2b3-46a6-aed1-311ce11e8ba4",
					"diagramNodeId": "50d27edd-cc9e-4ffb-b101-47ed6733e521",
					"simStepLabel": "Worker Thread Attempts Memory Map",
					"simStepDescription": "A worker thread receives a file path. Before searching, it calls `searcher.search_file()`, which checks the `MmapChoice` configuration. Because `mmap` is enabled, it attempts to open the file using a memory map.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/searcher/src/searcher/mod.rs",
						"startLine": "686",
						"endLine": "689",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"self.config.mmap.open",
							"file",
							"path",
							"mmap"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"file_path\": \"./logs/large-events.log\", \"file_handle\": \"<File>\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"status\": \"attempting_mmap\", \"file_path\": \"./logs/large-events.log\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6bf6e40d-0459-4062-837b-7f7aaf4ac646",
					"diagramNodeId": "c0213efd-7314-413f-8a1c-e1159cc69aa2",
					"simStepLabel": "Passing File Handle for Mapping",
					"simStepDescription": "The `search_file` function passes the file handle and path to the `MmapChoice::open` method to perform the memory mapping operation.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/searcher/src/searcher/mod.rs",
						"startLine": "686",
						"endLine": "686",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"self.config.mmap.open"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"file\": \"<File>\", \"path\": \"./logs/large-events.log\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"file\": \"<File>\", \"path\": \"./logs/large-events.log\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ecb4222e-b8cf-452c-a513-7ec478d405c0",
					"diagramNodeId": "52ce1885-7c83-4d59-bdff-23f1bb97e227",
					"simStepLabel": "Memory Map Creation",
					"simStepDescription": "The `MmapChoice::open` method verifies that memory maps are enabled via the configuration. It then calls `Mmap::map(file)` from the `memmap` crate. If the operating system successfully maps the file into the process's address space, an `Mmap` object is returned.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/searcher/src/searcher/mmap.rs",
						"startLine": "65",
						"endLine": "86",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"open",
							"is_enabled",
							"Mmap::map",
							"mmap"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"file\": \"<File>\", \"path\": \"./logs/large-events.log\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"Mmap\": {\"status\": \"success\", \"size\": 157286400}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "dc87abd5-f7d5-4e81-b907-9d0dc81a8780",
					"diagramNodeId": "3f2ab0e4-bf45-434a-93b4-aeeadffca912",
					"simStepLabel": "Returning Mmap Object",
					"simStepDescription": "The successfully created `Mmap` object, which represents the file's contents in memory, is returned to the `search_file` function.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/searcher/src/searcher/mmap.rs",
						"startLine": "80",
						"endLine": "80",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"Some(mmap)"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"Mmap\": {\"status\": \"success\", \"size\": 157286400}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"Mmap\": {\"status\": \"success\", \"size\": 157286400}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "da0d44b6-c6a4-4225-b58f-f376a56fbed5",
					"diagramNodeId": "f529c8cd-56d1-48ad-a512-f0f7defe5412",
					"simStepLabel": "Search Memory-Mapped Slice",
					"simStepDescription": "Because `mmap.open()` returned a valid `Mmap` object, `search_file` proceeds to call `self.search_slice()`. This function executes the regex search directly against the memory slice, avoiding the need to read the file into an intermediate buffer on the heap, which is highly efficient for large files.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/searcher/src/searcher/mod.rs",
						"startLine": "688",
						"endLine": "689",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"search_slice",
							"matcher",
							"mmap",
							"write_to"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"matcher\": \"<RegexMatcher>\", \"mmap_slice\": \"&[u8]\", \"sink\": \"<Printer>\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"search_result\": \"ok\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d2a75f16-c0b5-4c7b-8637-00e059aeeb19",
					"diagramNodeId": "83819a4c-f73e-4503-a339-1dc4682b4083",
					"simStepLabel": "Sending Matches to Sink",
					"simStepDescription": "As `search_slice` finds matching lines within the memory-mapped data, it sends each match to the configured `Sink`. In ripgrep, the sink is typically a `Printer` responsible for formatting the output.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/searcher/src/searcher/core.rs",
						"startLine": "334",
						"endLine": "338",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"sink.matched"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"SinkMatch\": {\"line_number\": 12345, \"bytes\": \"[ERROR] 2023-10-27T10:30:00Z: Database connection failed.\", \"matches\": [[0, 5]]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"SinkMatch\": {\"line_number\": 12345, \"bytes\": \"[ERROR] 2023-10-27T10:30:00Z: Database connection failed.\", \"matches\": [[0, 5]]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f25b1366-166b-4aeb-b0ed-76556649a3cb",
					"diagramNodeId": "93ce1fc0-3e9b-4006-bd90-19e2b12360cf",
					"simStepLabel": "Printing Results",
					"simStepDescription": "The `Printer` sink receives the match data. It formats the line with colors, line numbers, and file paths as configured, and writes the final output to a thread-safe buffer. This buffer is then flushed to standard output, displaying the search results to the user.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/main.rs",
						"startLine": "171",
						"endLine": "174",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"args.printer",
							"bufwtr.buffer"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"SinkMatch\": {\"line_number\": 12345, \"bytes\": \"[ERROR] 2023-10-27T10:30:00Z: Database connection failed.\", \"matches\": [[0, 5]]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"stdout\": \"logs/large-events.log:12345:[ERROR] 2023-10-27T10:30:00Z: Database connection failed.\\n\"}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- Performs recursive directory search in parallel by default, leveraging modern multi-core processors for significant speed improvements</li><li>- The <code>main</code> function in <code>crates/core/main</li><li>rs</code> dispatches to <code>search_parallel</code> when more than one thread is available</li><li>- Automatically uses memory maps (<code>mmap</code>) for searching large single files to improve performance, which is configurable via the <code>--mmap</code> flag</li><li>- Parallelism is managed by <code>ignore::WalkParallel</code> and threads are coordinated using <code>crossbeam</code></li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
