		"Utilize the PCRE2 regex engine for advanced features like look-around and backreferences": {
			"name": "Utilize the PCRE2 regex engine for advanced features like look-around and backreferences",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "b001bc82-d7e1-49ab-a45d-63ffedf1c538",
					"diagramNodeId": "4ec77cd0-0718-4dc0-b655-1da844ab75e4",
					"simStepLabel": "1. Parse `--pcre2` Command-Line Flag",
					"simStepDescription": "The user executes `ripgrep` with the `-P` or `--pcre2` flag to enable the PCRE2 regex engine. The flag parsing logic identifies this switch and updates the application's internal argument configuration.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/defs.rs",
						"startLine": "5375",
						"endLine": "5381",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"Flag",
							"PCRE2",
							"update",
							"args",
							"EngineChoice::PCRE2"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"command\": \"rg\", \"args\": [\"-P\", \"(?<=<li>)item\", \"index.html\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"engine\": \"PCRE2\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "41560cc1-7be4-4776-aa80-28b666b2856d",
					"diagramNodeId": "bd08bc31-79b5-41c4-b72f-1f982dbf6c67",
					"simStepLabel": "2. Transmit Parsed Engine Choice",
					"simStepDescription": "The parsed arguments, now indicating the user's choice to use the PCRE2 engine, are passed from the low-level argument parser to the high-level argument handler for further processing.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "374",
						"endLine": "374",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"EngineChoice::PCRE2"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"engine\": \"PCRE2\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"engine\": \"PCRE2\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "74cdd5d3-6b51-4c17-9dbe-7749bab1fe82",
					"diagramNodeId": "8c0413a7-6389-4cf3-b267-6c20b31e8f41",
					"simStepLabel": "3. Select PCRE2 Matcher",
					"simStepDescription": "Based on the `EngineChoice::PCRE2` value in the arguments, the application's logic branches to a specific function responsible for constructing a regex matcher using the PCRE2 engine. The `auto` option also exists, which would try the default engine first and fall back to PCRE2 on compilation failure.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "370",
						"endLine": "386",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"matcher",
							"self.engine",
							"EngineChoice::PCRE2",
							"self.matcher_pcre2()"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"HiArgs\": {\"engine\": \"PCRE2\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"function_call\": \"self.matcher_pcre2()\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6bdeb4e1-c75c-491a-9a32-0d8b1a923323",
					"diagramNodeId": "e5f83134-7c9e-4b1e-9fe6-11442cc8ada6",
					"simStepLabel": "4. Forward Patterns to PCRE2 Builder",
					"simStepDescription": "The regex patterns and other configuration options (like case sensitivity) are passed to the PCRE2 matcher builder function.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "415",
						"endLine": "415",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"matcher_pcre2"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"patterns\": [\"(?<=<li>)item\"], \"case_sensitive\": true, \"jit_enabled\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"patterns\": [\"(?<=<li>)item\"], \"case_sensitive\": true, \"jit_enabled\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "62233f98-5f45-4d39-b8ef-c973da11c758",
					"diagramNodeId": "b9bd4cec-b0f5-4d8d-bd5f-d7b1f9ad1969",
					"simStepLabel": "5. Configure and Build PCRE2 Matcher",
					"simStepDescription": "The `grep-pcre2` crate's `RegexMatcherBuilder` is instantiated and configured. Options such as JIT (Just-In-Time) compilation are enabled if available to improve performance. The builder then compiles the provided regex patterns into a usable `RegexMatcher` instance.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "418",
						"endLine": "443",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"builder",
							"grep::pcre2::RegexMatcherBuilder",
							"jit_if_available",
							"builder.build_many",
							"PatternMatcher::PCRE2"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"patterns\": [\"(?<=<li>)item\"], \"fixed_strings\": false, \"case_mode\": \"Sensitive\", \"jit_if_available\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"PatternMatcher\": \"PCRE2(RegexMatcher)\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "2d7b834e-8129-49d6-a0a9-9e6856693240",
					"diagramNodeId": "5f587f6a-71bd-43ec-8897-c472b079ccbb",
					"simStepLabel": "6. Propagate Compiled Matcher",
					"simStepDescription": "The compiled PCRE2 matcher, wrapped in a `PatternMatcher` enum, is returned to the main search logic to be used by the search worker.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/search.rs",
						"startLine": "198",
						"endLine": "198",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"PatternMatcher::PCRE2"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"PatternMatcher\": \"PCRE2(RegexMatcher)\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"PatternMatcher\": \"PCRE2(RegexMatcher)\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ba7e0d80-75c9-474f-aad3-ee3d141b6ca7",
					"diagramNodeId": "83de0dc6-071d-4f66-ae7f-3fef41b2fd41",
					"simStepLabel": "7. Dispatch Search to PCRE2 Implementation",
					"simStepDescription": "The search worker receives the file path to be searched and the compiled matcher. It checks the `PatternMatcher` enum variant and dispatches the search call to the function that uses the PCRE2 `RegexMatcher` implementation.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/search.rs",
						"startLine": "344",
						"endLine": "345",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"self.matcher",
							"PCRE2(ref m)",
							"search_path"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"matcher\": \"PatternMatcher::PCRE2(instance)\", \"path\": \"index.html\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"result\": \"search_path(pcre2_matcher, ...)\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "0c7a5f6f-7e72-467f-a7fc-441d1d90276b",
					"diagramNodeId": "b9bf9f98-f6b7-469a-8e6d-9a6f874ad69b",
					"simStepLabel": "8. Execute Search",
					"simStepDescription": "The generic searcher function is called, passing the specific PCRE2 matcher instance, the file path, and a 'sink' object responsible for handling and printing matches.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/search.rs",
						"startLine": "382",
						"endLine": "382",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"searcher.search_path"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"matcher\": \"pcre2_matcher_instance\", \"path\": \"index.html\", \"sink\": \"StandardSink\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"matcher\": \"pcre2_matcher_instance\", \"path\": \"index.html\", \"sink\": \"StandardSink\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6a0d0b01-cff5-447b-9126-9882fee3297f",
					"diagramNodeId": "1b8df61d-c161-4bb7-8f36-7b60820c8c77",
					"simStepLabel": "9. Find Matches in File",
					"simStepDescription": "The searcher reads the file's content and uses the provided PCRE2 matcher's `find_at` method (from the `grep-matcher` trait) to identify occurrences of the pattern. Because PCRE2 is being used, advanced features like the look-behind `(?<=<li>)` in the pattern are correctly processed.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/pcre2/src/matcher.rs",
						"startLine": "228",
						"endLine": "253",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"Matcher",
							"find_at"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"file_content\": \"<ul>\\n<li>item 1</li>\\n</ul>\", \"pattern\": \"(?<=<li>)item\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"match\": {\"start\": 9, \"end\": 13, \"text\": \"item\"}}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>- Opt-in to using the powerful PCRE2 regex engine with the <code>-P</code>/<code>--pcre2</code> flag</li><li>- Enables support for advanced regex features not available in the default engine, such as look-arounds (<code>(?<=</li><li>)</code>) and backreferences (<code>\\1</code>)</li><li>- The <code>crates/pcre2</code> crate provides the <code>RegexMatcher</code> implementation for this feature, which is conditionally compiled</li><li>- The <code>--auto-hybrid-regex</code> flag can automatically switch to PCRE2 if the pattern requires its advanced features</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
				"4ec77cd0-0718-4dc0-b655-1da844ab75e4": {
					"simStepIds": [
