		"Replace matched text in the output with new text, including capture group references": {
			"name": "Replace matched text in the output with new text, including capture group references",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "737b4594-f05a-4364-aa55-1ef7fab5ae40",
					"diagramNodeId": "9a174586-50ee-48d2-b47d-c3911a03119e",
					"simStepLabel": "Parse '--replace' Argument",
					"simStepDescription": "The command-line interface parses the input arguments, identifying the `-r` or `--replace` flag and its associated replacement string. This string is stored in an arguments struct for later use.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/defs.rs",
						"startLine": "5967",
						"endLine": "6036",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"struct Replace",
							"impl Flag for Replace",
							"update(v: FlagValue, args: &mut LowArgs)"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"args\": [\"rg\", \"(ticket)-(\\d+)\", \"-r\", \"item: $2, user: $1\", \"file.txt\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"patterns\": [], \"replace\": \"item: $2, user: $1\", \"positional\": [\"(ticket)-(\\d+)\", \"file.txt\"]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "43539604-968a-4968-a6c1-26ee641911cb",
					"diagramNodeId": "3d0a7b6c-5fb7-49af-acd6-f7ed5e04465c",
					"simStepLabel": "Transmit Parsed Arguments",
					"simStepDescription": "The parsed replacement string is passed from the low-level argument parser to the high-level argument handler, which prepares configurations for other components like the printer.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "976",
						"endLine": "1006",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"Patterns::from_lowargs"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"replace\": \"item: $2, user: $1\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"LowArgs\": {\"replace\": \"item: $2, user: $1\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "87174d16-5d77-402d-b09b-bcd88b34b5de",
					"diagramNodeId": "5d83f4af-db25-4c71-8317-27d5cbf2da80",
					"simStepLabel": "Configure Printer with Replacement String",
					"simStepDescription": "The high-level argument handler uses the replacement string to configure the `StandardBuilder`. The builder stores the replacement string in its configuration, which will be used to create the printer sink.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
						"startLine": "620",
						"endLine": "628",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"self.replace",
							"builder.replacement"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"HiArgs\": {\"replace\": \"item: $2, user: $1\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"StandardBuilder\": {\"config\": {\"replacement\": \"[105, 116, 101, 109, 58, 32, 36, 50, 44, 32, 117, 115, 101, 114, 58, 32, 36, 49]\"}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "84a73e2d-c815-4663-8744-d398d2a607da",
					"diagramNodeId": "e331d461-e40c-4ead-8f93-9bd36e1cdf0d",
					"simStepLabel": "Pass Match Data to Printer Sink",
					"simStepDescription": "As the searcher finds matches in a file, it sends each match result (as a `SinkMatch` object) to the printer's sink function for processing and output.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/printer/src/standard.rs",
						"startLine": "776",
						"endLine": "776",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"sink_match"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"SinkMatch\": {\"bytes\": \"ticket-123\", \"line_number\": 1, \"absolute_byte_offset\": 0, \"matches\": [{\"start\": 0, \"end\": 10}]}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"SinkMatch\": {\"bytes\": \"ticket-123\", \"line_number\": 1, \"absolute_byte_offset\": 0, \"matches\": [{\"start\": 0, \"end\": 10}]}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "bebc0274-fcfd-425d-91f2-160c6f551f30",
					"diagramNodeId": "4ca89a94-e328-4aeb-8515-45ccb701cf74",
					"simStepLabel": "Initiate Replacement Process in Sink",
					"simStepDescription": "The printer sink receives the match data. It checks its configuration, sees that a replacement string is defined, and calls the `Replacer` utility to perform the substitution.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/printer/src/standard.rs",
						"startLine": "740",
						"endLine": "758",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"replace",
							"self.replacer.replace_all"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"SinkMatch\": {\"bytes\": \"ticket-123\"}, \"Config\": {\"replacement\": \"item: $2, user: $1\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"call_to\": \"self.replacer.replace_all\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b7497dbb-aa8f-42f9-a95e-ce7dbd1e9889",
					"diagramNodeId": "816cc43f-51b4-407b-8df9-1d12d4fa167c",
					"simStepLabel": "Transfer Data to Replacer Utility",
					"simStepDescription": "The raw bytes of the matched line, the replacement string, and the matcher are passed to the `replace_all` method of the `Replacer` struct.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/printer/src/util.rs",
						"startLine": "50",
						"endLine": "61",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"replace_all",
							"haystack",
							"replacement"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"haystack\": \"ticket-123\", \"replacement\": \"item: $2, user: $1\", \"matcher\": \"...\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"haystack\": \"ticket-123\", \"replacement\": \"item: $2, user: $1\", \"matcher\": \"...\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d2bc60fd-f612-4d8a-84cd-e6047becc03b",
					"diagramNodeId": "c3846db4-1ff4-4054-82c9-2f32f2c517f4",
					"simStepLabel": "Interpolate Capture Groups",
					"simStepDescription": "The `Replacer` iterates over each match and uses the `interpolate` utility. This function parses the replacement string for capture group references (e.g., `$1`, `$2`, `$name`), looks up the corresponding captured text from the current match, and builds the final substituted string.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "crates/matcher/src/interpolate.rs",
						"startLine": "7",
						"endLine": "59",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"interpolate",
							"replacement",
							"append",
